module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.memo_key_rehashes_a_growing_persistent_value

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data memo_key_rehashes_a_growing_persistent_value: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "memo_key_rehashes_a_growing_persistent_value" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a memoized pure fold carries a growing persistent Map, but the memo demand key recursively hashes the contents of each fresh root. Sharing inside the value does not share its content hash across roots. A constant-cost map update is surrounded by a growing key-construction cost, and successive keys retain successive argument values. HARM: an otherwise incremental census becomes quadratic in identifier count before it can report its first corpus result.",
    "INSTANCE: v1_interpreter.eval_pure_named_call constructs eval_recompute_key before lookup or admission. Composite argument identity is content-hashed with allocation-local hash reuse; a new persistent Map root is a new allocation. tools.cause_assertion_census.cause_identifier_counts exposes this cost while consuming the parser's already-acquired Token stream. INSTRUMENT: tools.cause_identifier_cost_probe.probe, invoked with gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/cause_identifier_cost_probe.dag --function probe --arg report=/tmp/cause-identifier-cost. Each begin/end output pair brackets identifier counting after fixture construction; its file modification times expose the cost curve and its payload verifies the resulting key cardinality. Timings are derived from this instrument, not transcribed here.",
    "REALIZATION SELECTION: extdeps.realization.eval_memo declares GUNBC_EVAL_MEMO=0 a diagnostic recompute realization with identical semantics. The census invocation discloses that selection. tools.cause_assertion_census.bounded_census supplies the bounded module-identity control: run the same production and witness subjects under both realizations and compare complete rows by declaration identity, including all fields and identity refusals. Agreement of counts alone is not semantic agreement.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable by diagnosis and realization selection. The found condition is repeated whole-value memo-key construction over fresh roots sharing unchanged persistent structure; no structural guard stops that work or the retention of successive argument roots. CURRENT MITIGATION: the disclosed census invocation selects extdeps.realization.eval_memo's existing recompute realization, avoiding memo-key construction on that invocation only. The bounded memo-on/off identity comparison is a semantic experiment, not containment of other memoized demands. The defect remains on retained memo-enabled paths.",
    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed for the declared population of memoized pure-call demands over persistent composite arguments. Unchanged shared structure must carry reusable key evidence, so a persistent update constructs key evidence only for changed structure; key retention must follow an explicit bounded demand lifetime rather than retain every successive argument root. This requires a producer and consumer contract for persistent-structure key evidence and retention ownership, missing at v1_interpreter.eval_recompute_key and eval_pure_named_call. An allocation-local hash cache on each fresh root does not provide that capability. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: every retained demand in that population consumes such evidence without re-traversing unchanged structure, and expired demand keys release their retained roots under the declared lifetime contract.",
    "PROGRAM REMEDY: retire the seed implementation rather than author a new seed cache or evaluator patch. RETIREMENT TRIGGER: v1_interpreter.eval_pure_named_call and eval_recompute_key are absent from EVERY retained demand path in the declared population, including tools.cause_assertion_census.census and other interpreted pure folds; moving the census alone to the native route does not establish retirement of this class. Interpreter retirement is the program remedy, not the property's attainable ceiling. This row admits no new cache, evaluator patch, or census-specific bypass.",
    "SECOND INSTANCE (2026-09-19, swift-newt-222, gunbc built at 488aa317 on srv1 arm64): the same key construction over a growing STRING rather than a persistent Map. extdeps.languages.json.parse threads the whole document through every recursive *_at(s, i) call and Value::Str is hashed in full per call (no allocation-local reuse exists for strings), so parsing is quadratic in document size on the memo-enabled realization; perf attributed 79 percent of parse-phase samples to the SipHash write under eval_pure_named_call, and the recompute trace on a 112 KB document reported keyed_calls=156685 distinct_keys=134565 duplicated_keys=545 wasted_ms=44 -- seconds of key building to avoid tens of milliseconds. Re-derive with tools.json_parse_cost_probe.probe, never from these figures.",
    "EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY (DESIGN 6b), read from the ladder downward: std.materialization_ladder rule 5 prescribes Recompute for a single undeclared pure demand and rule 1 prescribes Share, never Memoize, for a repeat whose least common ancestor is a shared-state frame. The eval-frame result memo (extdeps.realization.eval_memo, since deleted) was a provider whose scope was ONE such frame, so no demand it could see was ever discharged into it by the ladder -- its admitted population was empty by construction -- yet it derived an identity for every pure call before any admission question was asked. Both instances of this row are that one boundary: the identity was built where no judgment had asked for it. The symptom-link patches this row refused (an allocation-local hash reuse for strings, a name allowlist, an adaptive cache) all keep the boundary and cheapen the work done past it.",
    "REPAIR (the seed change this row admits because it DELETES a seed cache rather than authoring one): v1_interpreter.eval_pure_named_call now consumes the admission BEFORE identity. The two provider tiers that remain -- the cross-claim tier admitted by the resolved-declaration roster of v2.workflow.floor_pure_producer_share, and the parse-table memo admitted by the Memoize verdict carried on the table -- each decide admission first and derive their key only for an admitted demand; an undeclared single demand derives no identity, looks nothing up and retains nothing. The eval-frame result memo, its per-ctx realization switch GUNBC_EVAL_MEMO, its frame-exit eviction and its hit/miss counters are deleted with their provider row. The recompute-trace ledger (GUNBC_RECOMPUTE_TRACE=1) still derives identities, as the rule-4 measurement instrument it always was, and serves nothing.",
    "RUNG AFTER REPAIR, at the declared grain. For the population of UNDECLARED pure demands in the seed interpreter the class is STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE: no keying site exists on that route, and the enrolled control (v1_compiler tests/pure_demand_recompute_admission an_undeclared_single_pure_demand_derives_no_identity_and_is_never_served) reads the frame's argument-identity odometer back at zero and goes red when unconditional keying is restored, with the trace ledger as its positive control. For the DECLARED population -- a roster-admitted cross-claim producer whose argument is a growing persistent value -- the found condition still stands and this row's ceiling, next-rung trigger and program remedy are unchanged: the roster is bounded and reviewed, and a row whose argument grows is the admission criterion's serve-below-recompute test failing, not this class dissolving.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "eval_pure_named_call", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "argument_identities_derived", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
